    {
      "id": "p0141-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby noted that this is a reference to the famous Shakespeare quote, \"Alas, poor Yorick!\", which Hamlet says while holding a skull. The translator preserved this reference by quoting the same line from a Japanese translation of Hamlet. However, the translator also noted that the quote is less recognizable in Japanese and thus more likely to be missed by Japanese players.",
        "raw": "Toby noted that this is a reference to\nthe famous Shakespeare quote, \"Alas,\npoor Yorick!\", which Hamlet says\nwhile holding a skull. The translator\npreserved this reference by quoting\nthe same line from a Japanese\ntranslation of Hamlet. However, the\ntranslator also noted that the quote\nis less recognizable in Japanese and\nthus more likely to be missed by\nJapanese players.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08853944,
          0.26235,
          0.37681142,
          0.45808571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08612686,
          0.26163571,
          0.37814038,
          0.45915714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          10,
          14,
          16,
          18,
          19,
          20,
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Toby 指出，这引用了莎士比亚的名句“唉，可怜的约里克！”——哈姆雷特手持头骨时说的话。译者采用《哈姆雷特》日译本中对应的台词，保留了这个典故。不过，译者也指出，这句名言在日语中没那么耳熟，因此日本玩家更容易错过。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
